<h2>Bottom line</h2>
<p>A Texas hurricane can trigger separate wind, flood and TWIA claims, each with its own deadline and deductible. Report quickly, document everything, submit the NFIP proof of loss within 60 days, and know that licensed insurers generally must decide within 15 business days of getting what they asked for. If a dispute builds, use appraisal or get professional help before the 61-day notice and two-year lawsuit deadlines come into play.</p>
